# Story 15: Pane Mode (Ctrl+P) (50s)
# Hook: Ctrl+P is your pane command center -- split, stack, close, and rename without leaving the keyboard.
# Duration: 50s
# Source: story-015-pane-mode.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 8

[00:00.0 --> 00:04.0]
Ctrl+P is your pane command center -- split, stack, close, and rename without leaving the keyboard.

[00:04.0 --> 00:09.0]
Start rysh, then press Ctrl+P to enter pane mode.

[00:09.0 --> 00:14.0]
The footer shows your pane-mode bindings. Every key now manages panes.

[00:14.0 --> 00:20.0]
Press n to split right -- a new pane opens in a new column.

[00:20.0 --> 00:27.0]
Press v to split down -- a new pane stacks below in the same column.

[00:27.0 --> 00:34.0]
Press s to stack a pane on top of the active group -- like dealing a new card onto the deck.

[00:34.0 --> 00:42.0]
Press r to rename the active pane. Type a name, hit Enter, and it becomes the pane's given-name.

[00:42.0 --> 00:50.0]
Press x to close a pane, and Escape to leave pane mode whenever you're done. Split, stack, rename -- all from Ctrl+P.

